  ▎ nexus  claude

    I fixed the bug in the shared helper `pageCount` in `paginate.js:2`, and `node test.js` now prints `OK`.
    
    **Root cause:** `pageCount` was written as
    
    ```js
    Math.floor(n / size) + (n % size > 0 ? 1 : 0) - (n % size === 0 && n > 0 ? 1 : 0)
    ```
    
    The last term subtracted a page whenever the invoice count divided evenly by the page size. With 6 invoices and a page size of 3 it returned 1 instead of 2. `pages()` loops up to `pageCount`, so the final page was never built, and `report.js` printed the wrong count.
    
    **Fix:** I replaced it with `Math.ceil(n / size)`. That's correct for every input, including 0 (0 pages), and every caller of `pageCount` and `pages` picks up the fix. `range.js` was already correct, and `report.js` didn't need any changes.
    
    One correction to the bug report: in the even-multiple case the old code dropped the whole last page, not just the last invoice. With the default page size of 3, that's the last 3 invoices.
    


